//
// Inter-service gRPC contract for the Content Creation core domain
// (chora_creation database, Team 1 / Content). Surface: A+ Creator mode.
//
// LearningAtom is the PRIMARY AGGREGATE ROOT of the entire Chora platform —
// collections (LearningPath in Consumption, Course in Delivery) QUERY atoms;
// they NEVER own them (per ddd-enforcement aggregate-invariant #1).
//
// AtomRevision is APPEND-ONLY (aggregate-invariant #4) — never UPDATE or
// DELETE content in place. AppendRevision adds a new revision row.
//
// AI-assisted authoring: GenerateAtomsViaAI calls the Model Broker
// Router -> Gateway through the AI Kernel; output is validated by the
// 6-agent content gate (Validator -> Classifier -> Web Researcher ->
// Q&A Generator -> Evaluator -> Reporter) before atoms are persisted.
//
// KnowledgeGraph queries are exposed as gRPC for service-to-service
// traversal (Consumption Discovery mode). Learner-facing reads use
// GraphQL (chora-contracts/graphql/creation.graphql).
//
// Cross-DB queries FORBIDDEN — references to other domains use UUIDs
// without FK constraints (aggregate-invariant #3).
//
// Deployed in chora-content (Team 1 pool). mTLS via the service mesh;
// SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
